	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## Usage

Browse WaniKani progress via the `wk` keyword.

* `wk &lt;page&gt;` - open a page: `summary`, `levels`, `stats`, `accuracy`, `leeches`, `lessons`, `reviews`.
* Text after the page filters its rows, e.g. `wk lessons 水`.
* Delete the page name to go back to the menu.
* Pages load in the background: `Loading &lt;page&gt;…` shows until the data arrives, then cached pages open instantly.
* First row on every page is the page itself: &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; opens the dashboard, &lt;kbd&gt;⇥&lt;/kbd&gt; goes back.
* &lt;kbd&gt;⇥&lt;/kbd&gt; on Lessons or Reviews available in Summary opens that queue.

![WaniKani progress menu](images/about/main.png)

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the selected lessons, reviews, level, or dashboard item.

Search WaniKani subjects via the `wks` keyword. Type to filter radicals, kanji, and vocabulary.

![WaniKani subject search](images/about/search.png)

* &lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; Open the selected subject on WaniKani.

Open the Summary view to see your current WaniKani progress.

![WaniKani progress summary](images/about/summary.png)

Set the keywords and API token in the [Workflow's Configuration](https://www.alfredapp.com/help/workflows/user-configuration/).

### Maintenance

* `:wk` - cache size (&lt;kbd&gt;↩&lt;/kbd&gt; reveals the folder) and Empty Cache.
</string>
